---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import '../styles/lab.css';

const site = Astro.site!;
const organizationSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'ResearchOrganization',
  name: 'Worldeology Lab',
  url: new URL('/', site).href,
  founder: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Xuanming Zhang' },
  description: 'Worldeology Lab studies Cognitive AI: systems that understand minds before action, inspect cognition during action, and model consequences after action.',
  knowsAbout: ['Cognitive AI', 'Theory of Mind', 'Metacognition', 'Interactive world models', 'Long-horizon AI evaluation']
};
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Worldeology Lab — Cognitive AI"
  description="Worldeology Lab studies the full cognitive trajectory: understanding minds before action, inspecting cognition during action, and modeling consequences after action."
  image="/og.png"
  imageAlt="Worldeology Lab — Cognitive AI from mind to action to world"
  headerTone="paper"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(organizationSchema)}></script>

  <main id="main" class="lab-site">
    <section class="lab-hero" aria-labelledby="lab-title">
      <div class="lab-hero-meta"><span>Independent research lab</span><span>London · Hangzhou · Everywhere cognition acts</span></div>
      <div class="lab-hero-copy" data-reveal>
        <p class="lab-kicker">Worldeology / Cognitive AI</p>
        <h1 id="lab-title">The answer is a point.<br /><em>Cognition is a trajectory.</em></h1>
        <p>We study AI systems that understand another mind before acting, inspect and revise their own cognition while acting, and model how their actions change the world afterward.</p>
        <nav aria-label="Explore Worldeology Lab"><a href="/research/">Read the research agenda ↗</a><a href="#work">Explore the work ↓</a></nav>
      </div>

      <div class="cognitive-orbit" aria-label="Cognitive AI spans before, during, and after an answer" data-reveal>
        <div class="orbit-ring orbit-ring-one"></div><div class="orbit-ring orbit-ring-two"></div>
        <div class="orbit-center"><span>The answer</span><strong>·</strong><small>one observable point</small></div>
        <article class="orbit-before"><b>01</b><span>Before action</span><strong>Understand minds</strong></article>
        <article class="orbit-during"><b>02</b><span>During action</span><strong>Inspect cognition</strong></article>
        <article class="orbit-after"><b>03</b><span>After action</span><strong>Model consequences</strong></article>
        <i class="orbit-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></i>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-definition" aria-labelledby="definition-title">
      <p class="lab-index">01 / Definition</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="definition-title">Cognitive AI 研究的，<br />是答案发生的整段过程。</h2>
        <div class="definition-copy">
          <p>我们花了很长时间教机器回答问题，亦或执行任务。更大的问题刚刚浮现：在指令接受之时，机器理解了什么？在推理形成之中，它能否察觉自己的偏离？当输出离开屏幕、进入人的生活之后，它又把世界推向了哪里？</p>
          <p>语言与场景只是认知短暂露出水面的部分。水面之下，有对他人意图的猜测、有权衡利弊的谋划、有无数推理路径在不确定性下收束。水面之外，行为参与现实，改变一个决定、一段关系，甚至一条原本不会发生的未来路径。</p>
          <p class="definition-line">答案是 AI 时代的一点。认知从这里开始，并继续向未来发生。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-program" id="research" aria-labelledby="program-title">
      <header><p class="lab-index">02 / Research program</p><h2 id="program-title">Before. During. After.</h2><p>Cognitive AI expands the unit of intelligence from an output to a revisable, consequential trajectory.</p></header>
      <div class="program-grid">
        <article data-reveal><span>Before the answer</span><h3>Infer what is not said.</h3><p>Model beliefs, desires, intentions, emotions, roles, and boundaries without confusing a hypothesis with a fact.</p><a href="/blog/MetaMind/technical-contribution/">MetaMind ↗</a></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>Inside the answer</span><h3>Find where thought diverges.</h3><p>Expose intermediate cognition, test it against context and values, then roll back to the point where another path remains possible.</p><a href="/research/#metacognition">Cognition-of-Thought ↗</a></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>Beyond the answer</span><h3>Follow what action changes.</h3><p>Track latent state, event chains, relationships, institutions, and future choices across persistent interactive worlds.</p><a href="/projects/mariolm/">MarioLM ↗</a></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-work" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <header><p class="lab-index">03 / Selected work</p><h2 id="work-title">One agenda.<br />Different instruments.</h2></header>
      <div class="work-list">
        <a class="work-row" href="/blog/MetaMind/technical-contribution/" data-reveal><span>2025</span><div><b>MetaMind</b><h3>Model the unspoken mind before response.</h3></div><p>Social cognition · Multi-agent metacognition</p><i>↗</i></a>
        <a class="work-row" href="/blog/MetaMind/cognitive-frontier/" data-reveal><span>2026</span><div><b>Cognition-of-Thought</b><h3>Make intermediate cognition inspectable and revisable.</h3></div><p>Process alignment · Reflective decoding</p><i>↗</i></a>
        <a class="work-row" href="/projects/mariolm/" data-reveal><span>2026</span><div><b>MarioLM</b><h3>Evaluate the future path an action creates.</h3></div><p>World models · Long-horizon interaction</p><i>↗</i></a>
        <a class="work-row" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.03999" data-reveal><span>2026</span><div><b>Long-Horizon Deception</b><h3>Audit behavior across an event chain, not a confession.</h3></div><p>AI safety · Social simulation</p><i>↗</i></a>
      </div>
      <a class="lab-text-link" href="/research/">View the full research map ↗</a>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-world" aria-labelledby="world-title">
      <div class="world-word" aria-hidden="true">WORLD·EOLOGY</div>
      <div class="world-copy" data-reveal><p class="lab-index">04 / The name</p><h2 id="world-title">The study of worlds as cognition and action continually remake them.</h2><p>Worldeology begins from a simple claim: intelligence cannot be understood only inside a model. It must also be studied in the beliefs it changes, the relationships it enters, and the futures it makes reachable.</p><a href="/about/">Why Worldeology ↗</a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-people-preview" aria-labelledby="people-title">
      <div><p class="lab-index">05 / People</p><h2 id="people-title">A research lab built around a field, not a product category.</h2></div>
      <article><img src="/assets/images/xuanming-zhang.webp" width="886" height="886" alt="Xuanming Zhang, founder of Worldeology Lab" loading="lazy" /><div><span>Founder</span><h3>Xuanming Zhang</h3><p>AI researcher working across metacognition, social intelligence, model mechanisms, and long-horizon interactive worlds.</p><a href="/people/">People and collaborators ↗</a></div></article>
    </section>

    <SiteFooter />
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
